# c6320 (2026-11-10): victim 4,6; Secondary = aggressor pool minus the victim threads and their siblings 32,34.
# HC HELD ON: applied at the ARM point and kept for the rest of the run, no
# control logic (thresholds below zero: HC_THETA_ON=-1 fires on the first armed
# tick, HC_THETA_OFF=-2 never releases). The "always on after 80 s" arm the
# user asked for (2026-11-01); also the unmatched arm for intrinsic overload.
# HarvestContainers with BANG-BANG control (motivation experiment, 2026-10-23).
# Apply on the FIRST tick with e_iso > HC_THETA_ON (HC_UP_WINDOWS=1) and a
# single threshold (HC_THETA_OFF == HC_THETA_ON; formula.go accepts equality).
# Release still waits HC_DOWN_WINDOWS ticks (100 ms each) under the
# threshold: HC removes the very contention that triggered it, so a
# zero-delay release would limit-cycle at the tick rate (each Apply/Restore
# re-registers with the Listener and restarts the Balancer). 50 = 5 s.
# Needs hc-listener running (qidlecpu loaded) on the node.
ISO_ACTUATOR=hc
N_MAX=0
HC_VICTIM_CPULIST=4,6
HC_SECONDARY_CPULIST=0,2,8,10,12,14,16,18,20,22,28,30,36,38,40,42,44,46,48,50
HC_TARGET_IDLE_CORES=1
HC_LOW_TIC=1
HC_ACBF=0.33
HC_MIN_SECONDARY_CORES=0
HC_BALANCER_CPU=24
HC_THETA_ON=-1
HC_THETA_OFF=-2
HC_UP_WINDOWS=1
HC_DOWN_WINDOWS=1000000
